# gate/relation-ownership.baseline — semantic relation identity owned by the
# AST layer. Pinned EXACTLY.
#
# THE LAW: the parser owns shape. It does not own semantic relation identity.
# Today it does anyway -- src/parser.zig:202 keeps a `relation_edges` map and
# src/parser.zig:2884 MINTS the semantic symbol as `"{name}__{level}"`. The
# real authority is src/relation.zig (`Id` at :320, `Names` at :354), and
# src/parser.zig:2941 already records the consequence: an edge declared in
# another module is not in the parser's map, so `mod.decode(u64)(v)` does not
# resolve. gap[025].
#
# The count below is the exact number of relation-identity tokens in each
# AST-layer file. It is a ceiling AND a floor: adding relation ownership to
# the parser fails, and paying it down fails until the number is re-pinned.
#
# Tokens counted: relation_edge relation_id RelationId relation_family
#                 relation_symbol
#
# Measured 2026-08-22 at idol@40de041c. Denominator: 8 AST-layer files
